1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,904
The missing voice arrived as an email from a remote terminal in a room nobody visited.

2
00:00:04,904 --> 00:00:09,788
I am the person whose address is in your release, it said.

3
00:00:09,788 --> 00:00:17,097
I never gave permission for the storage of my data, not once, and not in any form.

4
00:00:17,097 --> 00:00:22,821
There was no error in the technical sense; the error was in the mechanism.

5
00:00:22,821 --> 00:00:31,815
As a scientific matter, the execution of the instruction had been exact, and that was the problem.

6
00:00:31,815 --> 00:00:41,378
The platform had three menus, four packets of settings, and a translation of the consent form that nobody could read.

7
00:00:41,378 --> 00:00:52,047
A circuit of old machines, a tube of glue, and a sink full of cables: the lab had the look of an explosion in a chemistry set.

8
00:00:52,047 --> 00:00:58,866
The generator hummed, and the electronics on the shelf were covered in dust.

9
00:00:58,866 --> 00:01:05,289
The interaction between the input and the output had never been tested with a real person.

10
00:01:05,289 --> 00:01:20,342
A disc of old backups, a magnet beside the storage, and a prompt on the screen asking for a resolution: the whole apparatus had one weakness, and it was the human at the end of it.

11
00:01:20,342 --> 00:01:32,265
There was a fragmentation of responsibility: nobody owned the address list, and nobody could explain the absorption of personal data into a marketing outlet.

12
00:01:32,265 --> 00:01:46,492
The interpreter of the rules, a cracker of small puzzles, and the king of the local podcast all said the same thing: a service that cannot be explained cannot be consented to.

13
00:01:46,492 --> 00:01:55,905
Compatible systems, telecommunications, and a mechanism for withdrawal: those were the three things the person asked for.

14
00:01:55,905 --> 00:02:03,319
The force of the request was quiet, and the hope behind it was still there, waiting quietly.

15
00:02:03,319 --> 00:02:13,117
It was a scientific problem, and the science was not in the machinery; not one atom of the data had been taken with relaxation.

16
00:02:13,117 --> 00:02:23,055
The computer, the cell, the source, and the energy were all in the same attempt to build a program that technology could not quietly rewrite.

17
00:02:23,055 --> 00:02:34,832
Over the next billion operations, the club would have to pick one: the convenience of the system, or the consent of the person inside it.
